t Support Student Health Services Student Counseling Services Career Center Clubs & Recreation Dance Marathon Black Student Union Student Government Association Delta Alpha Pi Campus Activities Board Green Life PRISM Her Campus Ambrosians for Peace and Justice Sexual Assault Awareness Team Latinos Unidos About SAU About St. Ambrose History of SAU Catholic Values Campus Location Parking Davenport Christ the King Chapel Galvin Fine Arts Center Rogalski Center Multicultural House Wellness and Recreation Center Center for Health Sciences Education SAU Library Accreditation University Catalog News & Events News Events Faculty Office of the President Alumni Alumni Experience Ways to Give Visit Home / Tuition & Aid / Scholarships / School of Social Work Graduate Fellowships School of Social Work Graduate Fellowships Reducing costs for Master of Social Work students Explore eligibility details for the School of Social Work Graduate Fellowships, an opportunity for MSW students to reduce the cost of their degree. Apply to SAU School of Social Work Graduate Fellowships Details Each year, St. Ambrose University provides up to $2,500 to two MSW students through the School of Social Work Graduate Fellowships. Explore the requirements and application process below. School of Social Work Graduate Fellowships eligibility details Eligibility requirements for the School of Social Work Graduate Fellowships + School of Social Work Graduate Fellowships details The School of Social Work Graduate Fellowships are needs-based fellowships available to students enrolled in the Master of Social Work program. Recipients must be enrolled in 9 or more course credits planned for the Fall semester. Student eligibility and enrollment requirements: Enrollment in SAU’s Master of Social Work program Students should plan to take at least 9 credits in the Fall semester Apply to SAU Email Admissions School of Social Work Graduate Fellowships selection process + Two students each year are selected for the School of Social Work Graduate Fellowships. A committee of MSW faculty reviews applications for this award. Preference is given to students who demonstrate financial need, and recipients must be enrolled in at least 9 credits in the Fall semester. Apply to SAU Email Admissions Disbursement of scholarship funds + The School of Social Work Graduate Fellowships is disbursed following a straightforward process: The Master of Social Work Department shares a list of recipients with Financial Services. Disbursement occurs at the beginning of each year. Funds are directly credited to your account and applied toward tuition. Experience the seamless financial support of the School of Social Work Graduate Fellowships as you pursue your degree at St. Ambrose. Apply to SAU How to apply for the School of Social Work Graduate Fellowships Applying for a scholarship is easy. Follow these steps. Apply to SAU To qualify for the School of Social Work Graduate Fellowships, you need to apply to SAU’s MSW program and meet eligibility requirements. Apply to SAU Write your personal statement Prepare to submit a 500 word personal statement about your social work experience, academic performance, and stated financial need. Read the full prompt Submit your application Applications are due each year on April 15. Submit your application to be considered for the School of Social Work Graduate Fellowships. Apply by April 15 Other ways to reduce tuition Graduate assistantships We offer a number of graduate assistantships that can reduce your total tuition cost. Discover an affordable approach Transfer credits Transfer credits honor your previous coursework, fast-tracking your academic journey. Uncover the SAU difference Veteran/military benefits Discover benefits you qualify for and ease your transition to college with veteran/military benefits. Explore veteran/military benefits Become who you are meant to be Invest in your future. Contact SAU's Student Financial Aid to learn what assistance options are available so you can become who you're meant to be. Request information Apply now CONTACT US 518 W. Locust St. Davenport, IA 52803 admit@sau.edu FOLLOW US Area of Study Biology Business Criminal Justice Education Engineering Fine Arts Health Sciences Information Technology Liberal Arts Nursing Psychology Social Sciences About SAU Academic Calendar Bookstore Contact Us Employment Maps & Direction Pay My Bill Employee Login Strategic Plan College of Business Explore More Accessibility Healthcare Certificates Military News & Events Partner Universities Registrar SAU Library Mount Mercy FAQs Corporate Training Legal Consumer Information Institutional Review Board Site Map Title IX University Policies 2026 St. Ambrose University Terms of Use | Copyright | Non-Discrimination Statement"
