tudent Counseling Services Career Center Clubs & Recreation Dance Marathon Black Student Union Student Government Association Delta Alpha Pi Campus Activities Board Green Life PRISM Her Campus Ambrosians for Peace and Justice Sexual Assault Awareness Team Latinos Unidos About SAU About St. Ambrose History of SAU Catholic Values Campus Location Parking Davenport Christ the King Chapel Galvin Fine Arts Center Rogalski Center Multicultural House Wellness and Recreation Center Center for Health Sciences Education SAU Library Accreditation University Catalog News & Events News Events Faculty Office of the President Alumni Alumni Experience Ways to Give Visit Home / About SAU / Faculty St. Ambrose University Faculty Dedicated to prioritizing your learning experience With a wealth of experience and qualifications, our faculty is committed to fostering students’ academic success. They are ready to provide guidance, address questions and concerns, and provide an academic environment where you can thrive. Request information St. Ambrose faculty’s student-centered approach Our faculty has an unwavering dedication to innovative teaching philosophies and holistic educational experiences. They strive for an engaging and interactive learning environment that emphasizes a student-centric educational approach. With a commitment to student success, our professors use diverse and creative teaching methods. Hands-on experiences, discussions, and collaborative projects are designed to inspire critical thinking and equip students with practical life skills. Guidance and mentorship Our faculty provide guidance to students beyond coursework. They provide personalized advice and support to help students navigate their academic journeys. Through academic advising sessions, faculty members assist students with setting goals, exploring career paths, and making informed decisions. Faculty members are also involved in campus clubs, activities, and initiatives, which helps to foster a dynamic learning environment outside of the traditional classroom setting. SAU faculty directory Gain insight into the educators shaping St. Ambrose’s academic excellence by exploring our faculty directory. Each profile showcases information about each member’s academic background, area of expertise, ongoing research and contributions to their respective fields. Search by department, specialization or faculty name. Find faculty and staff members Supporting students every step of the way \"The ability to have direct, personal access to professors is a huge advantage of St. Ambrose. The professors care deeply about you and want you to succeed. You truly cannot beat the faculty and staff at St. Ambrose University, they are amazing!\" Kristina (Shelman) Rossmiller ‘20, BS in Biology Request information “From the moment you step foot on campus, you'll feel welcomed and supported by a tight-knit community of students, faculty, and staff. St. Ambrose offers a warm and inclusive environment where everyone can thrive academically, socially, and personally.” Zeinab Nehme ‘23,  MS in Speech-Language Pathology Request information \"St. Ambrose staff and faculty make it a priority to get to know each and every student and help them succeed in every way. It was comforting knowing they truly cared about my success and wanted to help me along the way.\" Katie Link ‘20, BA in Multimedia Journalism Request information ❮ ❯ ❮ ❯ Explore the possibilities at St. Ambrose At SAU, the Fighting Bees are encouraged to explore every opportunity to grow and learn, finally becoming the person they are meant to be. Call: 563-333-6000 Request information Apply now CONTACT US 518 W. Locust St. Davenport, IA 52803 admit@sau.edu FOLLOW US Area of Study Biology Business Criminal Justice Education Engineering Fine Arts Health Sciences Information Technology Liberal Arts Nursing Psychology Social Sciences About SAU Academic Calendar Bookstore Contact Us Employment Maps & Direction Pay My Bill Employee Login Strategic Plan College of Business Explore More Accessibility Healthcare Certificates Military News & Events Partner Universities Registrar SAU Library Mount Mercy FAQs Corporate Training Legal Consumer Information Institutional Review Board Site Map Title IX University Policies 2026 St. Ambrose University Terms of Use | Copyright | Non-Discrimination Statement"
